          "one_liner": "A self-cleaning textile that hosts a living, engineered microbial ecosystem within its fibers to continuously break down soil and odors with minimal moisture.",
          "concept_description": "This concept involves engineering textiles with embedded, living microorganisms that form a synergistic biofilm, analogous to a Schmutzdecke. These microbes would be selected or engineered to continuously break down sweat, oils, and odor-causing compounds using ambient humidity, thus creating a self-cleaning garment that rarely needs conventional washing. Advanced concepts include core-shell fiber structures to protect the microbes, enhancing fiber porosity to create ideal micro-environments, using fungal spores, or creating self-forming 'hotspots' that concentrate cleaning action where needed.",
