          "how_it_works": "1. The textile surface is designed or treated to promote the adhesion and growth of a specific, non-harmful microbial species or consortium. 2. This 'probiotic' biofilm colonizes the fabric, occupying the available space and consuming trace nutrients. 3. When the garment is exposed to undesirable microbes (e.g., from the environment or sweat), the established protective biofilm prevents them from attaching and proliferating through competitive exclusion. 4. This reduces the buildup of odor-causing bacteria and pathogens, extending the garment's wear time between washes.",
