          "how_it_works": "1. A flexible patch is constructed with a network of micro-channels on one side and a curated, living biofilm on the other. 2. The patch is applied to a soiled area of a garment. 3. A minimal amount of water is introduced into the microfluidic channels, which distribute it evenly to the biofilm, activating it without saturating the garment. 4. The activated biofilm degrades the stain with maximum efficiency. The microfluidics could also be used to deliver nutrients to 'recharge' the biofilm.",
