              "source_domain_summary": "The source is a comprehensive review of advanced wastewater treatment technologies. A key section focuses on using novel materials, such as stimuli-responsive polymers and nanofibers, to treat industrial effluents, particularly from the textile industry, by adsorbing and removing dyes and other contaminants from water.",
              "inspiring_principle": "Smart materials, specifically thermoresponsive polymers formed into electrospun nanofibers, can be engineered to have a high surface area for adsorbing contaminants (like dyes) and can then be triggered by an external stimulus (like temperature) to change conformation and release those contaminants, enabling a reusable capture-and-release system.",
