          "overall_synthesis": "The concept for an 'Adhesive Biofilm Cleaning Sheet' originates from a direct application of a fundamental principle in microbiology: the adhesive nature of a biofilm's Extracellular Polymeric Substance (EPS) matrix. The idea repurposes what is often a problem in industrial and medical settings—unwanted microbial adhesion or 'biofouling'—into a novel solution for waterless cleaning. By focusing on the physical property of stickiness rather than the metabolic activity of the microbes, the concept synthesizes the understanding of EPS as a natural bonding agent into a tangible product that physically lifts particulates from fabric, creating a new category of bio-inspired dry cleaning.",
