          "one_liner": "A peel-off sheet coated with a sticky biofilm that lifts away dirt and particulates from clothing without water.",
          "concept_description": "This concept is for a thin, flexible cleaning sheet coated with an adhesive biofilm. The sheet is pressed onto clothing to lift away particulate dirt and oils via adhesion, and is then peeled off for a completely dry cleaning process.",
          "how_it_works": "1. A disposable sheet is coated with a specially engineered biofilm that produces a high concentration of adhesive extracellular polymeric substances (EPS). 2. The sheet is pressed firmly onto a garment. The sticky EPS layer adheres to surface contaminants like dust, hair, and skin flakes. 3. The sheet is then peeled away, lifting the adhered contaminants off the fabric, similar to a lint roller but at a microbial scale. 4. The used sheet is discarded.",
