              "inspiring_principle": "Bacteria can be genetically engineered to produce specific functional agents (e.g., proteins, chemicals) and package them into their naturally secreted Outer Membrane Vesicles (OMVs), which then serve as stable, biocompatible nanocarriers for delivering that payload.",
