          "idea_title": "Inherent and Rechargeable Antimicrobial Textiles",
          "one_liner": "A fabric that actively inhibits microbial growth through embedded agents or surface structures, which can potentially be 'recharged' to extend its hygienic lifespan.",
          "concept_description": "This concept is for a textile with inherent, long-lasting antimicrobial properties that work passively to prevent the growth of odor-causing bacteria and other microbes. By keeping the garment hygienically cleaner for longer, the frequency of water-intensive washing is drastically reduced. Advanced versions may include self-healing properties to ensure durability or be 'rechargeable' with a simple, low-water treatment.",
