              "analogical_leap": "The creative leap was to reframe fabric not simply as a surface, but as a potential habitat for microbial communities. By viewing the challenge of keeping clothes clean through the lens of hospital surface contamination, the focus shifts from simply removing dirt to preventing the formation of the underlying, resilient biofilm structure that causes persistent odors and contamination.",
              "web_snippet_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0196655323000792",
              "web_snippet_title": "Klebsiella pneumoniae survives on surfaces as a dry biofilm ..."
