          "idea_title": "Appliance with Bio-Active Surfaces",
          "one_liner": "A washing appliance where the internal drum is coated with cleaning microbes, allowing it to purify fabrics with minimal water.",
          "concept_description": "This concept focuses on coating the internal surfaces of a washing appliance (e.g., the drum) with immobilized, living microbes. As clothes tumble with minimal water, they make contact with the bio-active surface, which degrades soil and purifies the small amount of process water.",
          "how_it_works": "1. The inner drum of a washing machine or a similar appliance is coated with a durable, resilient biofilm of cleaning microbes. 2. Clothes are tumbled in the machine with a very small amount of water, enough to dampen them and facilitate contact. 3. The constant contact between the clothes and the bio-active surface allows the microbes to degrade soil directly. 4. This approach places the cleaning 'engine' on the permanent hardware rather than in a consumable or on the garment itself.",
