        "inspiration_summary": "The conceptual breakthrough came from a direct analogical leap, asking: 'What if we could treat the organic soil on a t-shirt like industrial wastewater?' The inspiration was drawn from large-scale Bioelectrochemical Systems (BES) used for water purification [1]. We reimagined the industrial bioreactor as a countertop appliance and the fabric's soil matrix as the 'contaminated water' to be purified. The core principle of using a gentle electrical field to boost microbial activity was miniaturized and repurposed from an environmental technology into a consumer solution for rapid, low-impact fabric care.",
